title: 'Codegen: scope task records its error; together block yields scope error'
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: high
blocked_by:
- 2-6-5-1
created_at: '2026-06-13T19:29:53'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T20:31:33'
result: 'Wired child-task error to the scope (E1/E5). Scope-task bodies (anon dispatch)
  now type-propagate the RAW err variant (current_fn_ret_ty taken during body lowering)
  and their err enums are folded into the enclosing fn''s error types (collect_errreturn_enums),
  making it fallible. Codegen Return for scheduler tasks calls jinn_scope_record_current_error(errword).
  The together block, when its children can raise (HIR Together carries Vec<Symbol>
  errs), calls jinn_scope_join_take_error after join (returns err word or INT64_MIN),
  and on error reconstructs Result::Err via __scope_build_err_{enum} and re-raises
  via the enclosing fn''s error-return path. Runtime: added jinn_scope_record_current_error
  + jinn_scope_join_take_error (split jinn_scope_join into no-free core). New conformance
  tests failing_child_surfaces_error and failing_child_cancels_siblings pass (sibling
  cancelled at yield points, error surfaces, exit 0). Zero-warning build; concurrency_shutdown
  (18), error_effects (27), bulk_tests (912) all green. !! handler arm and multi-err
  reconstruction deferred to 2-6-5-3.'
description: 'Wire child-task error to the scope (E1/E5). When a scheduler task (anonymous
  dispatch / scope-owned actor handler) propagates an error out of its top frame,
  codegen must call jinn_scope_record_error(scope, err) instead of (or in addition
  to) the normal early-return. The scope task already returns via the early-return
  path; capture the propagated error value there. Make the `together` block lowering,
  after __scope_join, call jinn_scope_take_error and, if present, perform the function-level
  error propagation (implicit propagate at scope site) OR feed it into a quaternary
  `!!` arm if present (handled in 2-6-5-3). For now (no handler): a failing scope
  re-raises in the enclosing function via the existing early-return-with-error path.
  Depends on 2-6-5-1. DoD: a together block with a failing dispatch makes the enclosing
  fn fallible and the error surfaces; failing_child_cancels_siblings test passes (sibling
  does not complete its work). Atomic.'
